# /etc/paperbot/executor-wooxpro2.env  (root:root, chmod 600; made by an owner, never by install.sh)
# The keys of the SECOND WOO X Pro account (owners 10-24, docs/friend-bot-ko.md: a friend's account, its executor
# paperbot-executor-wooxpro2 follows the paper bot '친구 매매법'). systemd reads this file for that one unit INSTEAD of
# /etc/paperbot/executor.env, so the two WOO X Pro executors never see each other's keys. Never commit the real file,
# never paste a key in a chat: write it on the server with  sudoedit /etc/paperbot/executor-wooxpro2.env
#
# Only the lines below. Do NOT start from a copy of /etc/paperbot/executor.env: the executor ("own_keys": true) refuses
# to start when another exchange's key (BYBIT_*, MEXC_*, DEEPCOIN_* ...) is in its environment, and a key another
# executor's database has used (the owners' own WOO X Pro key) refuses it too.
#
# WOO X Pro, the second account: a key made in THAT account (API management) with "읽기 전용, 선물 거래" only, NO
# withdrawal, bound to this server's IP 158.247.200.152; the access key, the secret key and the memo written when the key
# was made (it is part of every signature).
WOOXPRO_LIVE_KEY=
WOOXPRO_LIVE_SECRET=
WOOXPRO_LIVE_MEMO=
# WOO X Pro cannot report a key's permissions through the API: after checking the key page (futures trade only, no
# withdrawal, IP bound), write exactly FUTURES_ONLY_NO_WITHDRAW_IP_BOUND here (the executor refuses to start without it)
WOOXPRO_LIVE_KEY_CHECKED=
# The mainnet switch: exactly I_UNDERSTAND, and only together with "mode": "mainnet" in executor-wooxpro2.json.
PAPERBOT_LIVE_MAINNET=
# Alerts: /etc/paperbot/live-telegram.env (the live bot's own token and the owners' private chats), loaded after this
# file by the unit, sets them; nothing to write here when that file has them. Without that file, remove the "#" and
# write the token and the chat ids (never leave a chat line empty: keep it commented out instead).
#TELEGRAM_BOT_TOKEN=
#TELEGRAM_CHAT_CRITICAL=
#TELEGRAM_CHAT_WARN=
#TELEGRAM_CHAT_INFO=
